 from Cumbria to the Cairngorms, and exploring the landscapes of Roger Deakin, J. A. Baker, Nan Shepherd and others, Robert Macfarlane shows that language, well used, is a keen way of knowing landscape, and a vital means of coming to love it. Praise for Robert Macfarlane: 'He has a poet's eye and a prose style that will make many a novelist burn with envy' John Banville, Observer \"I'll read anything Macfarlane writes\" David Mitchell, Independent 'Every movement needs stars. In [Macfarlane] we surely have one, burning brighter with each book.'","publicationYear":2015,"displaySummary":"In [Macfarlane] we surely have one, burning brighter with each book.'","primaryTopic":"Travel, Exploration & Place","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Nature & Environment","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Nature & Environment","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Nature & Environment","mappedSubject":"Nature & Environment","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily explores the relationship between language and landscape, focusing on nature and environment, while also encompassing elements of travel writing.","id":"subject-evidence-book-landmarks-robert-macfarlane-1"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Arts & Criticism","mappedSubject":"Arts & Criticism","score":2,"confidence":"low","note":"nature/environment keyword; arts/criticism keyword; travel/place keyword","id":"subject-evidence-book-landmarks-robert-macfarlane-4"},{"source":"award_category","rawLabel":"Wainwright Prize: Nature Writing","mappedSubject":"Nature & Environment","score":2,"confidence":"low","sourceId":"source-award-record-wainwright-nature-writing-wikipedia-wainwright-prize-shortlist-table-citing-annual-official-anno","id":"subject-evidence-book-landmarks-robert-macfarlane-3"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Nature & Environment","mappedSubject":"Nature & Environment","score":2,"confidence":"low"